{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["חמת תנינים — they deserved to drink from justice, were it not for desecration of the Name, lest they say: ״Our hand is exalted.״" "פתנים אכזר — a wicked person, as it is written: ״פתן חרש יאטם אזנו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Rashbam paraphrases the verse's 'wine of serpents' as a punishment YHWH's justice would have mandated; 'they' refers to Israel, and 'our hand is exalted' (cf. Deut. 32:27) is the enemy's boast that God avoided by not fully punishing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:54.158952611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}